<title>USA: USDA offers grain credit guarantees to Jordan.</title>
<headline>USDA offers grain credit guarantees to Jordan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA on Thursday said it was offering $40 million in credit guarantees for sales of U.S. wheat and feed grains to Jordan in fiscal 1997.</p>
<p>The export credit guarantees were made available under the GSM-102 program.</p>
<p>The department said it was making no dollar allocation to the specified commodities, to provide maximum flexibility to buyers and sellers, USDA said.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
</text>
